This folder contains unique job configurations used in the SE performance tests.

Each job configuration is known by it's unique file name.  It is very important that
this filename not change once it has been used, as this filename gets saved with the
performance results and will be used in queries to filter and return particular
performance data.

The naming convention being used is trying to clearly identify the purpose of the job,
followed by any clarifying features or remarks. e.g. a job may start with:
  "daily-"      to indicate that this job is repeatedly run on a periodic basis.
  "debug-"      to indicate that this job is purely for debugging purposes only.
  "experiment-" to indicate that something is being tried here and the results
                are likely a one-off.

Please think carefully about how jobs are named as they are saved in the database with
their configuration to guard against the case where a regular repeating job is unknowingly
changed in such a way that the results are affected. We need to ensure that configurations
are consistent and hence they should be treated as being immutable.